sonic-nixos changes to sonic-bgpcfgd for software BFD (FRR bfdd, no ASIC offload):
- BfdMgr: sessions active unless type=async_passive (as BfdOrch's SAI default);
  upstream makes every session without type passive, so two SONiC ends (or
  two VRFs of one switch) never come up.
- BGPPeerMgrBase.update_peer: a changed bfd / bfd_check_ctrl_plane_failure of an
  existing BGP_NEIGHBOR is applied live (upstream only handles admin_status).
- staticroutebfd: session timers from the environment (upstream: fixed 50 ms x3).
Applies to src/sonic-bgpcfgd.

--- a/bgpcfgd/managers_bfd.py
+++ b/bgpcfgd/managers_bfd.py
@@ -70,7 +70,9 @@
             'detect-multiplier': self.MULTIPLIER,
             'receive-interval_ms': self.RX_INTERVAL_MS,
             'transmit-interval_ms': self.TX_INTERVAL_MS,
-            'passive-mode': True,
+            # sonic-nixos: active unless type=async_passive, as BfdOrch's SAI
+            # sessions (no type = async_active); passive on both ends never comes up.
+            'passive-mode': False,
         }
 
     def redis_to_local_res(self, data):
@@ -104,10 +106,7 @@
             res_data["transmit-interval_ms"] = int(data["tx_interval"])
 
         if "type" in data:
-            if data["type"] == "async_active":
-                res_data["passive-mode"] = False
-            else:
-                res_data["passive-mode"] = True
+            res_data["passive-mode"] = data["type"] == "async_passive"
 
         return res_data
 
